B1  FINDINGS L2: 'J_Y ~ 0.13-0.18 nearly constant, i.e. g_obs ~ 6.9 g_N'
------------------------------------------------------------------------
    J_Y = s/Delta_req, so 1/J_Y = (g_obs - g_bar)/g_bar = M_dark/M_bar, and g_obs/g_N = 1 + 1/J_Y.
    headline J_Y range        : 0.1265 - 0.1838   (record '0.13-0.18'  OK)
    1/J_Y = M_dark/M_bar      : 5.44 - 7.91
    from the fitted law Delta = 5.47 s^0.811 over s in [0.09, 0.91]: 1/J_Y = 5.57 - 8.62, log-centre 6.93
    -> L2's own '.out' sentence 'G rescaled by 1/J_Y ~ 6.9' is CORRECT as a dark-to-baryon ratio.
    -> FINDINGS' restatement 'i.e. g_obs ~ 6.9 g_N' is NOT: g_obs/g_N = 1 + 1/J_Y = 7.93.

